**Test filters.** For this step these gates run only the tests their filter selects (plus any inherited expected-red tests); put the tests this step adds or changes where a filter value finds them:
- `constructor-unit-tests`: 

**How to implement.** The numbers one experiment is evaluated with at one parameter vector: each item's values and each opened material's crystal (001 §L 'Scope is the sharing rule'; 001 §I 'every sample made of it shares them (`MaterialScope`)'; step 361: `Sample.openedMaterialsIn` — 'the forward model reads it (S11.2)'). Each doc is one to three lines citing spec 0050 S11.2. In `StudyForward.fs`, after `parameterLayoutWith` (step 372): (1) `ExperimentAssignment = { itemValues : Map<ItemId, ParameterValues>; crystals : Map<MaterialVersionId, CrystalParameters> }`, with `member this.valuesOf (item : Item) : ParameterValues`, its entry or `ParameterValues.ofParameters item.parameters` (step 245) for an item the map lacks; `member this.crystalOf (material : OpenedMaterial) : CrystalParameters`, its entry or the copy's `currentCrystal` (step 361); and `member this.materialProxyOver (materials : MaterialProxy) : MaterialProxy`, `materials` with `resolveVersion` answering, for a version `crystals` holds, the entry the store answers with its `physics` replaced by `CrystalParameterPhysics` of the assignment's crystal (step 355), every other version and field passing through, so a stack sample made of an opened material is solved with the study's working copy. (2) `type StudyParameterLayout with member this.assignmentFor (study : Study) (items : Item list) (experiment : ExperimentName) (vector : StudyParameterVector) : Result<ExperimentAssignment, StudyForwardError>`: `VectorLengthErr` naming both lengths when the vector does not hold one value per entry; otherwise an entry's owner holds the experiment when it is an `ItemOwner` or a `MaterialOwner`, a `SessionOwner s` whose session of `this.sessions` lists it, or the `ExperimentOwner` of it, and (a) each of `items` takes `ParameterValues.ofParameters item.parameters` with each entry k on one of its parameters whose owner holds the experiment set by `withValue name (vector.valueAt k)` (step 245); (b) each of `study.materials` takes its `currentCrystal` with each such entry on one of its components written through the generated axis of that name (`crystal.parameterAxes`, `writeValue`, step 361); (c) then each of `study.links` (step 364) sets its follower to its leader's value in this assignment: an item parameter's `valueOf`, or a component read through its generated axis's `parameterValueOf`, written as in (a) or (b). `StudyForwardError` gains `VectorLengthErr of reason : string`, rendered `the parameter vector does not fit the study: <reason>`. No cache or option is added. Tests, in `StudyForwardTests`, over step 372's fixture and its layout: `an experiment's items take the vector's value for the owner that holds it, and every other parameter its own`: at [0.7; 2; 3; 1.6], E1's assignment gives CPL1 `c2.retardance` 0.7 and the Phone `gain` 2 and `darkOffset` its own 0, E3's gives `gain` 3, and every other parameter of each item is its own value. `an opened material's crystal takes its components from the vector, and a link's follower takes its leader's value`: E1's crystal of the opened version is the uniaxial copy with `n_o` 1.6 and its other three components the copy's; with CPL2 added (`c2.retardance` known at 1.2) and linked to follow CPL1's (step 364), CPL2's value is 0.7 at E1 and its known 1.2 in an assignment taken before the link. `a stack sample made of an opened material resolves to the study's working copy`: `materialProxyOver`'s `resolveVersion` of the opened version answers the entry whose physics is `CrystalParameterPhysics` of E1's crystal, and of another version the store's entry unchanged. `a vector of another length is refused`: a vector of three values answers `VectorLengthErr` naming 3 and 4. `every forward error renders its condition and its payload` covers `VectorLengthErr`.

**Acceptance.** After the assignment lands, `StudyParameterLayout.assignmentFor` MUST give each item the vector's value for the owner holding the experiment and its own value otherwise, each opened material its crystal from the vector, each link's follower its leader's value, and `materialProxyOver` MUST resolve an opened version to the working copy; constructor-unit-tests MUST pass, including `an experiment's items take the vector's value for the owner that holds it, and every other parameter its own`, `an opened material's crystal takes its components from the vector, and a link's follower takes its leader's value`, `a stack sample made of an opened material resolves to the study's working copy` and `a vector of another length is refused`, the count rising by 4, and the widened `every forward error renders its condition and its payload`; and build, elevation and the twenty s37 invariants MUST pass.
